#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Panel"
msgstr "Panèl"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; panel (often referred to as &kicker;) is the bar that you'll usually "
"find at the bottom of the screen when you start up &kde; for the first time. "
"For detailed help on &kicker;'s usage you can type <ulink url=\"help:/kicker\">"
"help:/kicker</ulink> in &konqueror; to read the user manual."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The panel gives you quick access to applications and makes it easier for you to "
"organize your desktop. Using the &kde; panel you can:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"launch applications using the <guimenu>K</guimenu> menu or the application "
"buttons"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "switch desktops using the panel's pager applet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "switch active windows, and minimize or maximize them"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "browse folder using the browser menu functionality"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"access panel applets that extend the panel's functionality, offering for "
"example mixers, clocks or a system monitor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "Arrangement"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Arrangement</guilabel> tab you can configure the size and "
"position of the panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have more than one panel on screen, you can select at the top of the "
"window which panel you wish to configure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the section labeled <guilabel>Position</guilabel> "
"is a set of 12 small buttons arranged in a square. Each button corresponds to a "
"location for the panel. Click on a button and notice where the panel is located "
"on the preview monitor to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Generally, the available space in kicker is used more efficiently if the panel "
"is aligned horizontally, &ie; attached to the top or bottom screen border."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the section labeled <guilabel>Length</guilabel>, you can use the combo box "
"and slider to adjust the <emphasis>minimum</emphasis> "
"length of the panel. If you place a mark in the checkbox labeled <guilabel>"
"Expand as required to fit contents</guilabel>, the panel will become longer if "
"more space is needed. When less space is required on the panel, the panel will "
"shrink down to the minimum size. If there is no mark in the checkbox, then the "
"panel is fixed to the length specified in this section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The final section of this table is labeled <guilabel>Size</guilabel>"
", and refers to the <emphasis>height</emphasis> of the panel. The panel's size "
"can be <guilabel>Tiny</guilabel>, <guilabel>Small</guilabel>, <guilabel>"
"Medium</guilabel>, <guilabel>Large</guilabel> or <guilabel>Custom</guilabel>"
". If you choose <guilabel>Custom</guilabel> mode, you can resize &kicker; by "
"specifying a height in the combobox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have multiple monitors, you can configure the panel for each screen "
"entirely independently. If you are not sure which screen is which, Press the "
"<guibutton>Identify</guibutton> and a number will appear centred on each "
"screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then simply choose the screen you wish to configure from the drop down box "
"labelled <guilabel>Xinerama screen</guilabel>, or choose <guilabel>"
"All Screens</guilabel> to have identical configurations on each."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hiding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on your screen resolution you may find that the panel takes away too "
"much of your precious screen real estate. To save screen space, the panel "
"offers manual hiding of the panel, an auto hide feature, and the ability to "
"allow other windows to lay on top of the panel. These features are selected in "
"the section entitled <guilabel>Hide Mode</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Hide Mode</guilabel> section has three options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Only hide when panel-hiding button is clicked"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this option is selected, the panel will remain visible at the location you "
"defined unless you click on the button at the far right (for horizontally "
"oriented) or bottom (for vertically oriented) button. This button has an arrow "
"on it pointed to the edge of the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once clicked, the panel will disappear. If the button is clicked again, the "
"panel will re-appear at the same location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hide automatically"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, then the panel will automatically disappear after "
"the number of seconds specified in the combo box below the option. To make the "
"panel reappear, simply move the mouse pointer to the edge of the screen where "
"the panel is located, and the panel will reappear immediately."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you place a mark in the checkbox labeled <guilabel>"
"Show panel when switching desktops</guilabel>, the panel will automatically "
"reappear when you switch desktops. (The panel will disappear again after the "
"specified number of seconds.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allow other windows to cover the panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As this option's label implies, the panel is always on the desktop when this "
"option is selected. It is now possible, however, for application windows to lay "
"on top of the panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To restore the panel, simply move the mouse cursor to the screen location "
"specified in the drop box labeled <guilabel>Raise when the pointer touches the "
"screen's:</guilabel>. You can change this value by selecting one of the choices "
"provided in the drop down box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once the panel has moved back on top of the application window, it will stay "
"there until an application window becomes active again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The next section down is labeled <guilabel>Panel-Hiding Buttons</guilabel>"
". It consists of two check boxes: <guilabel>Show left panel-hiding "
"button</guilabel> and <guilabel>Show left panel-hiding button</guilabel>"
". Use these checkboxes to show and hide the left and right manual panel hiding "
"buttons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If there is no mark in the checkbox labeled <guilabel>"
"Animate panel hiding</guilabel>, then whenever the toolbar is hidden, is simply "
"disappears. If there is a mark in the check box, then the panel appears to "
"slide off the edge of the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can determine how quickly the panel appears to move by adjusting the slider "
"from <guilabel>Fast</guilabel> to <guilabel>Slow</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menus"
msgstr "Menuts"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Menus</guilabel> tab you can configure the panel menu's "
"behavior. This affects the K menu you will often use to launch applications, "
"the browser menus you can use to access folders and other menus like the recent "
"documents menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>K Menu</guilabel> frame offers you some options to configure the "
"<guimenu>K</guimenu> menu's functionality. This frame consists of 4 items:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Menu item format:</guilabel> radio buttons have three options. "
"This determines how the application name (&ie; &konqueror;, &kword;, &etc;) and "
"the description (&ie; Web Browser, Word Processor, &etc;) are displayed on the "
"&kmenu;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Optional Menus</guilabel> checkboxes allow you to determine which "
"special menu items appear in the &kmenu;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Bookmarks</guilabel> menu allows you to quickly select from the "
"same bookmarks that are available in &konqueror;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Find</guilabel> menu offers access to the &kfind; application to "
"search for local files, and a quick link to a search engine to search for "
"things on the Internet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Konqueror Profiles</guilabel> menu allows you to launch "
"&konqueror; with any of your configured profiles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Network Folders</guilabel> menu can launch a &konqueror; file "
"manager window displaying any of your configured network folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Preferences</guilabel> menu allows you to launch each &kcontrol; "
"module directly from the K menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Print System</guilabel> menu provides several menu entries to "
"help manage the printer(s) attached to your system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Quick Browser</guilabel> menu gives you quick links to locations "
"on your hard drive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Recent Documents</guilabel> menu lists the most recently edited "
"documents and will automatically launch the application to edit or view this "
"document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>System</guilabel> menu allows you quick access to some commonly "
"visited places, including your Home folder, and the Trash. You may find this "
"useful instead of having a separate entry for each of these in the &kmenu;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Terminal Sessions</guilabel> menu provides menu items to launch "
"several different types of terminal programs (command line interfaces)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Show side image</guilabel> will add a small image to the side of the "
"menu. This is purely decorative."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:218
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guibutton>Edit K Menu</guibutton> button launches the &kde; menu editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>QuickBrowser Menus</guilabel> area you can configure whether "
"the panel's browser menus will show hidden files or not (hidden files on &UNIX; "
"systems are those whose filenames begin with a dot) as well as how many files "
"at most will be shown in a browser menu. The latter option may be especially "
"useful if you have a rather small screen resolution, as then the browser menus "
"will quickly fill up your screen when you browse folders containing many files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The quick start section in the K menu offers quick access to programs you have "
"used often or recently. In the <guilabel>Quick Start Menu Items</guilabel> "
"frame you can choose whether this section will show the most recently or the "
"most frequently used programs. Using the option <guilabel>"
"Maximum number of entries</guilabel> combo box, you can configure how many "
"programs the quick start section will remember."
msgstr ""

